aracterized as a “Retrieve-Read” framework [7]."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_d833c861b460e226","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"RETRIEVAL In the context of RAG, it is crucial to efficiently retrieve relevant documents from the data source."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_254d88d884f262a6","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":18,"quote":"Sabharwal, “Interleav- ing retrieval with chain-of-thought reasoning for knowledge-intensive multi-step questions,” arXiv preprint arXiv:2212.10509, 2022."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_1308fdf0c0219e76","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":12,"quote":"Evaluation Aspects Contemporary evaluation practices of RAG models empha- size three primary quality scores and four essential abilities, which collectively inform the evaluation of the two principal targets of the RAG model: retrieval and"},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_5a8ae7af32a9d1fc","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"However, Naive RAG encounters notable drawbacks: Retrieval Challenges."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_c54c628c79a678ac","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":5,"quote":"Once the knowledge from the retrieval results is judged to be inaccurate, it is unwise to still get stuck in it, which is likely to result in fabricated facts."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_6533fbe5b1c7ba0d","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":10,"quote":"Using our framework, practitioners can adjust how often retrieval occurs using the token probability of reward tokens."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_5d935a95fdca83be","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":3,"quote":"These reflection tokens (Table 1) signal the need for retrieval or confirm the output’s relevance, support, or completeness."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_1561f63effe8dae8","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":5,"quote":"3.3 Metrics We report retrieval and QA performance on the datasets above using recall@2 and recall@5 (R@2 and R@5 below) for retrieval and exact match (EM) and F1 scores for QA performance."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_001a2a33b33b706d","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":77,"quote":"Interleaving retrieval with chain-of-thought reasoning for knowledge-intensive multi-step questions."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_412eb8faa6586cd7","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":6,"quote":"5.2 Baselines We primarily compared CRAG with both ap- proaches with and without retrieval, where the latter can be further split into standard RAG and latest advanced RAG, including: Baselines without retrieval."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"dc0ae3c5584ed146_c_2830a2a1c4514610","docId":"dc0ae3c5584ed146","docTitle":"2212.10496_Precise_Zero_Shot_Dense_Retrieval_without_Relevance_Labels","page":2,"quote":"Later works studied the second stage pre-training of language model speciﬁcally for retrieval (Izacard et al., 2021; Gao and Callan, 2021; Lu et al., 2021; Gao and Callan, 2022; Liu and Shao, 2022)."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_631ee40ed880cfed","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":23,"quote":"Additionally, we note that there is some correlation better OpenIE and retrieval performance, given that the 8B Llama-3.1-Instruct version performs worse that its 70B counterpart in both retrieval and intrinsic metrics."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_254d88d884f262a6","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":18,"quote":"Catanzaro, “Retrieval meets long context large language models,” arXiv preprint arXiv:2310.03025, 2023."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_4a7de899de607c3d","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":16,"quote":"Interleaving retrieval with chain- of-thought reasoning for knowledge-intensive multi-step questions."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_181c8bf27b0b14b3","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"4 Results 4.1 Measuring and reporting performances As mentioned earlier, we used three proxy tasks the study chunking. We cannot directly assess the quality of retrieval at the chunk level due to the lack of ground-truth at the chunk level."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_26249f4bdc41b629","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":9,"quote":"Retrieval can be viewed as two tasks: classification and ranking."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_cdd36691fb020a53","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":5,"quote":"Similarly, approaches like Generate-Read [13] replace tradi- tional retrieval with LLM-generated content, while Recite- Read [22] emphasizes retrieval from model weights, enhanc- ing the model’s ability to handle knowledge-intensive tasks."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3025ebdcb9ebb485","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"In general, retrieval of KGs has two stages: identifying seed entities and retrieving facts or entities."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_02847529579e8b88","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":8,"quote":"While our method outperforms other baselines, on PopQA or Bio, powerful instruction-tuned LMs with retrieval (e.g., LLama2-chat, Alpaca) show large gains from their non-retrieval baselines."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_c54c628c79a678ac","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":5,"quote":"Correct Here, a retrieval is assumed Correct when the confidence score of at least one retrieved document is higher than the upper threshold."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_589bc4e8cae01e02","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":2,"quote":"Section III focuses on optimization methods in retrieval,including indexing, query and embedding optimization."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e2ab10a48622bc45","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":4,"quote":"ial cues.2 Finally, as is done when the hippocampal signal is sent upstream, we aggregate the output PPR node probability over the previously indexed passages and use that to rank them for retrieval."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_254d88d884f262a6","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":18,"quote":"Manning, “Raptor: Recursive abstractive processing for tree-organized retrieval,” arXiv preprint arXiv:2401.18059, 2024."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_05a521270f216026","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"Chunks are then encoded into vector representations using an embedding model and stored in vector database. This step is crucial for enabling efficient similarity searches in the subsequent retrieval phase."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_5a03cbc1c12462e6","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":10,"quote":"Like these works, HippoRAG shows the potential for synergy between these two technologies, combining the knowledge graph construction abilities of LLMs with the retrieval advantages of structured knowledge for more effective RAG."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_3ed5b3a93800017b","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":13,"quote":"Active retrieval augmented generation."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_54f654d3ebc5bda8","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":10,"quote":"Word embedding based gen- eralized language model for information retrieval."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_6450d43634bcc2d0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":2,"quote":"Given a new query, HippoRAG identifies the key concepts in the query and runs the Personalized PageRank (PPR) algorithm [30] on the KG, using the query concepts as the seeds, to integrate information across passages for retrieval."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_14d6cbd4379965a1","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":5,"quote":"It is well known that global signals for word importance, like inverse document frequency (IDF), can improve information retrieval."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_4eb522b69751bf59","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":24,"quote":"E.2 Qualitative Analysis In Table 10, we show three more examples from three different domains that illustrate HippoRAG’s potential for solving retrieval tasks that require such cross-passage knowledge integration."},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f2896d5f55e04d17","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"The Memory module leverages the LLM’s memory to guide retrieval, creating an unbounded memory pool that 5 aligns the text more closely with data distribution through iter- ative self-enhancement [17], [18]."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_05a521270f216026","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"This step is crucial for enabling efficient similarity searches in the subsequent retrieval phase."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_1308fdf0c0219e76","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":12,"quote":"Standard metrics from the domains of search engines, recommendation systems, and information retrieval systems are employed to measure the performance of the RAG retrieval module."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2185ad1e9a647f92","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"RAG Robustness The presence of noise or contradictory information during retrieval can detrimentally affect RAG’s output quality."},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2185ad1e9a647f92","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"These results underscore the importance of developing specialized strategies to integrate retrieval with language generation models, highlighting the need for further research and exploration into the robustness of RAG."},{"id":"c39","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2e7f7273fa816f48","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"On one hand, providing LLMs with a large amount of context at once will significantly impact its inference speed, while chunked retrieval and on-demand input can significantly improve operational efficiency."},{"id":"c40","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_39a5dda334fd31c5","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"• Schema Retriever, a trained model to extract schema components relevant to input text in the same vein as information retrieval."},{"id":"c41","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_784801446a75a137","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"In this work, we introduce HippoRAG, a novel retrieval framework inspired by the hippocampal indexing theory of human long-term memory to enable deeper and more efficient knowledge integration over new experiences."},{"id":"c42","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_d125f8e7fcbac0e3","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"For FEVER [56] fact veriﬁcation, we achieve results within 4.3% of state-of-the-art pipeline models which use strong retrieval supervision."},{"id":"c43","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_42da8a29bcae98c7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":1,"quote":"It meticulously scrutinizes the tripartite foundation of RAG frameworks, which includes the retrieval, the generation and the augmentation techniques."},{"id":"c44","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_a156781ad74e225a","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":1,"quote":"However, existing work utilizes the generative ability of LLMs for In- formation Retrieval (IR) rather than direct pas- sage ranking."},{"id":"c45","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_795da409fe24f385","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":1,"quote":"Ragas: Automated Evaluation of Retrieval Augmented Generation Shahul Es†, Jithin James†, Luis Espinosa-Anke∗♢, Steven Schockaert∗ †Exploding Gradients ∗CardiffNLP, Cardiff University, United Kingdom ♢AMPLYFI, United Kingdom"},{"id":"c46","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_f295172e59b25157","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":1,"quote":"However, RAG fails on global questions directed at an entire text corpus, such as “What are the main themes in the dataset?”, since this is inherently a query- focused summarization (QFS) task, rather than an explicit retrieval task."},{"id":"c47","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_347747745d362e3f","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":2,"quote":"For retrievers, conventional RAG assumes the target information is indexed in an image or text corpus, which can be uniformly represented as vector embeddings and enable one-size-fits-all embedding-based retrieval."},{"id":"c48","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_8faf205d52225055","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":2,"quote":